So if I'm understanding correctly, I can permute 1 gene for a genome-wide lod threshold for all genes, as long as I account for the multiple testing across all genes? If this is the case, do I still need to transform gene expression to normal quantiles? I ask because I assume that if I do so, the actual eqtl mapping would have to rely on quantile normalized expression values as well, which I have found significantly changes the eqtls.

P.s., I'm using a variance stabilizing transformation on the expression values in order to perform things like PEER hidden factor analysis, and found that quantile normalization on top of vst was giving me strange eqtls.

